EPHEMERIS

Ephemeris is a local C++ command-line system for filing-aware momentum
research.  It builds a SQLite database from SEC filings and price history,
materializes an investable universe, ranks stocks by momentum, applies a
small Markov regime throttle, and writes portfolio targets and backtest
results back to the database.


REQUIREMENTS

        C++17 compiler
        SQLite development library
        libcurl development library
        pkg-config
        make

SEC commands also need a real user agent:

        EPHEMERIS_USER_AGENT='name email@example.com'
        export EPHEMERIS_USER_AGENT


BUILDING

        make

This builds the ephemeris executable in the source directory.

        make test

This runs a deterministic fixture pipeline through the real command-line
program and checks expected outputs.

        make dist

This creates dist/ephemeris-v0.1.0.tar.gz from the tracked source tree.

        make clean

This removes generated build output.


SYNOPSIS

        ephemeris db init --db DB
        ephemeris sec sync-companies --db DB
        ephemeris sec sync-submissions --universe FILE --db DB
        ephemeris sec sync-companyfacts --db DB
        ephemeris sec update --db DB
        ephemeris securities import-history --input FILE --db DB
        ephemeris prices import --input FILE --db DB
        ephemeris universe build --date DATE --db DB
        ephemeris universe explain --date DATE --ticker TICKER --db DB
        ephemeris signal momentum --date DATE --db DB
        ephemeris signal explain --date DATE --ticker TICKER --db DB
        ephemeris regime filter --date DATE --db DB
        ephemeris portfolio build --date DATE --top N --db DB
        ephemeris portfolio explain --date DATE --db DB
        ephemeris audit database --db DB
        ephemeris audit prices --db DB
        ephemeris audit asof --date DATE --db DB
        ephemeris backtest --from DATE --to DATE --db DB
        ephemeris report --date DATE --db DB


DESCRIPTION

Ephemeris keeps the database as the durable system boundary.  Each command
does one job, writes materialized rows, and emits plain tab-separated output.
The database can be inspected directly with sqlite3 and the command output is
usable with ordinary shell tools.

The main pipeline is:

        SEC submissions and company facts define companies and filings.
        Adjusted prices define tradability and momentum.
        Universe construction records eligibility by date.
        Momentum ranks eligible securities by date.
        The regime filter estimates current momentum risk.
        Portfolio construction writes target weights.
        Backtests write NAV and trade records.


DATABASE

Initialize a database:

        ./ephemeris db init --db data/ephemeris.db

The schema stores companies, securities, filings, XBRL facts, prices,
universe membership, signals, regime features, regime outputs, portfolio
targets, backtest NAV, and backtest trades.


SEC DATA

Build or refresh the company and security master from SEC's public company
ticker feed:

        ./ephemeris sec sync-companies \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

This fetches:

        https://www.sec.gov/files/company_tickers_exchange.json

It writes companies, securities, and security_identifier_history.  Use --limit
for a small trial database and --asof to set the valid_from date explicitly.

Synchronize recent SEC submissions for a ticker list:

        ./ephemeris sec sync-submissions \
                --universe data/universe/tickers.txt \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

If --universe is omitted, sync-submissions updates the companies already
stored in the database.

Synchronize compact company facts for known CIKs:

        ./ephemeris sec sync-companyfacts \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Run a repeatable SEC update:

        ./ephemeris sec update \
                --db data/ephemeris.db \
                --limit 100

This runs sync-companies and sync-submissions.  Add --facts to also run
sync-companyfacts.  A full --facts update can be slow because SEC companyfacts
is one request per CIK.

The same flow is available as a script:

        scripts/update-sec-db data/ephemeris.db --limit 100

The submissions command resolves tickers through the SEC company ticker feed,
downloads submission JSON, stores company records, and stores recent filings.

The companyfacts command downloads SEC companyfacts JSON and stores a compact
set of accounting tags for revenue, net income, assets, liabilities, equity,
shares, cash, and debt.


SECURITY HISTORY

Import ticker to CIK history:

        ./ephemeris securities import-history \
                --input data/raw/security-history.csv \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Expected CSV columns:

        ticker,cik,valid_from,valid_to,source

Universe construction resolves CIK through security_identifier_history as of
the rebalance date before checking filings or share-count facts.


PRICE DATA

Import adjusted prices from CSV:

        ./ephemeris prices import \
                --input data/raw/prices.csv \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Expected CSV columns:

        date,ticker,open,high,low,close,adj_close,volume,market_cap

The market_cap column may be empty.  If it is empty, universe construction
tries to combine the latest SEC share count with adjusted price.

Parquet is intentionally outside the executable.  Convert Parquet upstream
with DuckDB or Arrow tooling and pass Ephemeris CSV.

A deterministic fixture can be generated with:

        scripts/make-fixture-prices > /tmp/ephemeris-prices.csv


UNIVERSE

Build a point-in-time universe:

        ./ephemeris universe build \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --min-market-cap 2000000000 \
                --min-adv 20000000 \
                --min-price 5 \
                --require-current-filing \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Universe rows are materialized by date.  This prevents later signals and
backtests from silently recomputing eligibility with current metadata.

Explain a stored universe decision:

        ./ephemeris universe explain \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --ticker AAPL \
                --db data/ephemeris.db


MOMENTUM

Rank eligible securities:

        ./ephemeris signal momentum \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --lookbacks 63,126,252 \
                --skip-days 21 \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

The default score is:

        0.50 times 12-month momentum excluding the most recent month
        0.30 times 6-month momentum excluding the most recent month
        0.20 times 3-month momentum excluding the most recent month
        minus 0.25 times 3-month realized volatility

Explain a stored signal and the prices used in the score:

        ./ephemeris signal explain \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --ticker AAPL \
                --db data/ephemeris.db


REGIME FILTER

Estimate current regime probabilities:

        ./ephemeris regime filter \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --market SPY \
                --model models/momentum_regime.model \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

The regime layer is a small Markov throttle:

        three hidden states: favorable, neutral, stress
        sticky transition probabilities
        transition tilt from trend, volatility, breadth, concentration,
        and drawdown
        heavy-tailed emission scoring
        filtered probabilities only
        continuous exposure rather than hard state switching

The stored output is:

        p_favorable
        p_neutral
        p_stress
        expected_momentum_edge
        exposure

Model parameters are loaded from a plain text model file.  The default tracked
model is:

        models/momentum_regime.model

When a regime output is stored, Ephemeris also stores model metadata in the
regime_models table.


PORTFOLIO

Build target weights:

        ./ephemeris portfolio build \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --top 50 \
                --max-weight 0.04 \
                --regime-model models/momentum_regime.model \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

The first portfolio is long-only and equal-weighted after the regime exposure
throttle.  Unused exposure is written as CASH.

Explain stored target weights:

        ./ephemeris portfolio explain \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --db data/ephemeris.db


BACKTEST

Run a monthly top-N backtest:

        ./ephemeris backtest \
                --from 2015-01-01 \
                --to 2026-01-01 \
                --top 50 \
                --cost-bps 10 \
                --cost-model models/cost_default.model \
                --regime \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Without --regime, the backtest uses full exposure.  With --regime, each
rebalance stores filtered regime probabilities and uses the resulting exposure
throttle.

The cost model is a plain text file.  The default tracked model is:

        models/cost_default.model

If --cost-model is omitted, the backtest uses --cost-bps as a simple inline
slippage assumption.


AUDIT

Audit database integrity:

        ./ephemeris audit database \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Audit price coverage and obvious price problems:

        ./ephemeris audit prices \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Audit a specific as-of date:

        ./ephemeris audit asof \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

Audit output is tab-separated and intentionally count-oriented.  It is meant
to catch silent wrongness before adding more research features.


REPORT

Print a compact report:

        ./ephemeris report \
                --date 2026-04-01 \
                --db data/ephemeris.db

The report prints universe counts, regime probabilities, top signals,
portfolio weights, and latest NAV as tab-separated text.


FILES

        Makefile
                Build rules.

        README
                Plain text project documentation.

        docs/DATA-REALISM
                Data realism priorities and staging tables.

        models/momentum_regime.model
                Default regime throttle parameters.

        models/cost_default.model
                Default transaction cost model.

        scripts/make-fixture-prices
                Deterministic sample price generator for tests and examples.

        src
                Focused C++ translation units for CLI, database, SEC, prices,
                universe, signals, regime, portfolio, backtest, and reports.

        tests/smoke.sh
                End-to-end command smoke test used by make test.

        LICENSE
                MIT license.

        CONTRIBUTING
                Contribution and development notes.

        ephemeris.db
                Default SQLite database path if --db is omitted.


EXIT STATUS

        0       success
        1       command error, bad input, unavailable network resource, or
                database failure


NOTES

This is an MVP research appliance, not a broker.  It does not place orders.

The useful edge is expected to come from data discipline: point-in-time
eligibility, clean security classification, realistic prices, and explicit
materialized outputs.  The Markov model is only a capital throttle.
